      "comment": "See THE SPLIT-TAG CONTRACT above. \"[fli\" matches nothing and \"rty] hi\" contains no \"[\" at all, so the joined buffer carries a visible \"[flirty] hi\" for one frame; the terminal frame's authoritative text is stripped as a whole and repairs it. The third text event IS the repair — an implementation that only emitted the completion would leave the leaked copy on screen.",
